   "id": "q127",
   "system": "full",
   "answer": "Plasma branched-chain amino acid levels are elevated in people with insulin resistance and type 2 diabetes, with elevated levels strongly associating with insulin resistance [2]. The underlying mechanisms of elevated plasma branched-chain amino acid levels on insulin-stimulated glucose uptake in humans remain largely unknown, but it is hypothesized that dysfunctional branched-chain amino acid catabolism may be an underlying factor [3].",
