   "system": "full",
   "answer": "The hazard ratio for colorectal cancer associated with diabetes in the mostly African American, low-income cohort was 1.47 [1]. This association was greater for participants without recent colonoscopy screenings (HR, 2.07; 95% CI, 1.16-3.67) and with smoking history (HR, 1.62; 95% CI, 1.14-2.31), potentially due to cancer screening differences.",
