   "system": "full",
   "answer": "Pancreas density was lower in patients with type 2 diabetes than in control subjects, in accordance with existing data, with a mean density of 30 HU in patients with type 2 diabetes and 35 HU in control subjects [1]. This lower density is associated with a higher fat content, suggesting that the pancreas of patients with type 2 diabetes was probably fattier than the controls' [1].",
